[1t[6n[c[?1004h[?9001h[33mcommit 6511ce791386e73e49d9a4708c3da693c61be8ee[m
Author: devusr <devusr@localhost>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 01:36:28 2026 +0300

    Agent-friendly rendering cost, fresh session environment, daemon generations
    
    - in-place changes swap instantly: a ticking spinner costs 9 frames/s and
      0.5% CPU instead of 103 frames/s and 5.7%
    - rows keep their history when only part of the screen scrolls
    - sessions get the launching window's environment, scrubbed
    - socket name carries a generation so incompatible builds never share a daemon
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

